{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"id":"call_IcLWeCZMfSfMFw2S8xEsrD4w","input":{"checked":{"basis":"Reviewed PR #121 at 2871d9e against origin/main, with focused reads of the playtest probes, pause stack, Jmodot clock and ResourceExts, their callers and tests. Jmodot worktree matches the PR pointer. Skills: architecture_philosophy read; Cx/Engine/test rules auto-loaded. Memory: searched review/agent-playtest and Jmodot GameClock/pause concepts.","stoppedAt":"blocked","toolsUsed":["Read","Grep","Glob","Bash","semantic-search"]},"findings":[{"agent":"nmrpcnb-code-reviewer","action":"FIX","category":"bug","critical":true,"file":"Playtest/Probes/FixtureItem42.cs:34","description":"The input driver inherits the floor's pausable process mode. A scripted `pause_wasd` press makes `FixtureItem38` pause the tree, after which the driver cannot release the press, send an unpause step, or reach `QuitAfterSeconds`; the scripted run hangs.","old":"public override void _Ready()\n    {\n        if (Steps == null)","new":"public override void _Ready()\n    {\n        ProcessMode = ProcessModeEnum.Always;\n        if (Steps == null)","scope":["Playtest/Probes/FixtureItem42.cs","Tests/Integration/Playtest/FixtureItem43.cs"],"rationale":"Strong (read): `Global/Lifecycle/FixtureItem38.cs:92-107` pauses on the authored pause action, while this probe's `_Process` drives both subsequent input and quitting. Keep the driver running under tree pause and update its process-time documentation and a pause/unpause integration test."},{"agent":"nmrpcnb-code-reviewer","action":"FIX","category":"bug","file":"Playtest/Probes/FixtureItem01.cs:136","description":"A foreign pause claim acquired after a step window opens leaves `_stepWindowOpen` true and ticks pending. `OpenStepWindow` returns without detecting the new pause, so `IsHeld` stays false and the playtest command's hold poll times out instead of cancelling the step.","old":"if (_stepWindowOpen)\n        {\n            return;\n        }","new":"if (_stepWindowOpen)\n        {\n            if (GetTree().Paused)\n            {\n                JmoLogger.Error(this, $\"[FixtureItem01] step cancelled: another pause holder took over ({DescribePausingOverlays()})\");\n                _stepTicksRemaining = 0;\n                CloseStepWindow();\n                _stack.ClaimPause(this);\n                _claimed = true;\n            }\n            return;\n        }","scope":["Playtest/Probes/FixtureItem01.cs","Tests/Integration/Playtest/FixtureItem02.cs"],"rationale":"Strong (read): `FixtureItem01.cs:136-139` skips the only foreign-pause check when a window is open; `Tests/Integration/Playtest/FixtureItem02.cs:219-239` tests only a claim held before opening. Add the mid-window case and restore the global physics-step cap when cancelling."},{"agent":"nmrpcnb-code-reviewer","action":"FIX","category":"bug","file":"Playtest/Probes/FixtureItem42.cs:76","description":"Two non-overlapping steps for the same action can become due in one process frame. The loop presses both before the first can be released, so the second action edge is lost and the first later release can cut off the second hold.","old":"while (_pending.Count > 0 && _elapsed >= _pending[0].AtSeconds)","new":"while (_pending.Count > 0 && _elapsed >= _pending[0].AtSeconds\n            && !_held.Any(h => h.Step.Action == _pending[0].Action))","scope":["Playtest/Probes/FixtureItem42.cs","Tests/Integration/Playtest/FixtureItem43.cs"],"rationale":"Strong (read): validation at lines 52-60 accepts a zero-length hold followed by the same action 0.01 seconds later; both are due in a 60 Hz frame, but releases run only before the press loop. Defer the second press until the next frame releases the first, and test coalesced due steps."},{"agent":"nmrpcnb-code-reviewer","action":"FIX","category":"bug","critical":true,"file":"Jmodot/Implementation/Shared/GameClock.cs:55","description":"A duplicate clock replaces `Current` with a fresh zero-time clock while the original keeps ticking. Removing the duplicate then clears `Current` despite the original still being live, making every `NowSeconds`/`NowMsec` reader throw; the new test explicitly pins this state.","old":"JmoLogger.Warning(this, $\"[GameClock] A second GameClock entered the tree ('{Name}'); the newer one is now Current.\");","new":"JmoLogger.Error(this, $\"[GameClock] duplicate clock '{Name}' rejected; keep the existing game-time source.\");\n            ProcessMode = ProcessModeEnum.Disabled;\n            QueueFree();\n            return;","scope":["Jmodot/Implementation/Shared/GameClock.cs","Tests/Integration/Shared/FixtureItem26.cs"],"rationale":"Strong (read): `GameClock.cs:55-69` changes and then clears the sole required clock; `Tests/Integration/Shared/FixtureItem26.cs:166-187` asserts the resulting null even though the original remains. Reject duplicates and change the test to preserve the original clock rather than resetting game time."},{"agent":"nmrpcnb-code-reviewer","action":"PLAN","category":"bug","file":"Playtest/Probes/FixtureItem21.cs:44","scope":["Playtest/Probes/FixtureItem21.cs","Tests/Integration/Playtest/FixtureItem22.cs"],"description":"Capture retains every full-resolution image until the strip is written. The allowed 240 frames at the command's 1280×720 resolution alone require roughly 844 MiB of RGBA pixel storage, before the sheet, duplicates and running game; higher resolutions can exhaust memory.","rationale":"Strong (read): `_frames` stores full `Image` objects, `RecordSample` only appends, and `Save` clears the list after all frames and the sheet are written. Stream full-resolution PNGs as they arrive and retain only bounded thumbnails and manifest metadata; pin peak retention, not just the after-save count."},{"agent":"nmrpcnb-code-reviewer","action":"PLAN","category":"bug","file":"Jmodot/Implementation/Shared/ResourceExts.cs:132","scope":["Jmodot/Implementation/Shared/ResourceExts.cs","Tests/Logic/JmodotTests/ResourceExtsSetForwardedSlotTests.cs","Visual/Presentation/FixtureItem36.cs"],"description":"`SetForwardedSlot` assigns the new Resource and disconnects the old one before attempting a connection that can fail. If `Connect` rejects the callable or incoming resource, the method throws with the slot changed and its change forwarding absent; callers such as `FixtureItem36.Lit` never emit their own change notification.","rationale":"Strong (read): assignment precedes `Rewire` at lines 131-133; `Rewire` disconnects at 197-200 and throws on failed connect at 204-209. Make replacement transactional—connect first, preserve the old slot/forwarding on failure, then disconnect and publish—and test a rejected ObjectID-bound callable."}],"gaps":["The supplied CONTEXT has a changed-file list and statistics, not the promised full diff and full file contents. The origin/main PR changes 364 parent files plus 30 Jmodot files; this single seat could not read every changed file or apply every checklist item. Findings are limited to files and call sites actually read; a batched full-scope review remains required.","The context's three cited `.claude/plans/*.md` files are absent from the PR worktree and untracked there, so source-to-plan coverage could not be verified. No build or runtime suite was run in this review."]},"name":"StructuredOutput","type":"tool_use"}],"usage":{"input_tokens":200948,"output_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"timestamp":"2026-09-25T16:31:07.560Z"}
